<BaseLayout title="Secure AKS Service Blueprint">
  <h1>Secure AKS Service Blueprint</h1>
  <p class="muted">Production-oriented reference implementation demonstrating secure CI/CD, AKS workload identity, Kubernetes deployment patterns, observability and software supply-chain security.</p>

  <h2>Problem</h2>
  <p>The blueprint shows how to build, test, containerise and deploy a small service to AKS with production concerns: secure CI/CD, SBOM generation, vulnerability scanning, and minimal runtime privileges.</p>

  <h2>Architecture & approach</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Terraform for infrastructure examples (resource groups, ACR, AKS, Key Vault).</li>
    <li>Helm chart for Kubernetes deployment with secure defaults.</li>
    <li>Workload identity and Key Vault CSI integration for secrets.</li>
    <li>SBOM generation and Trivy scanning during CI.</li>
    <li>Prometheus metrics and structured JSON logging for observability.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Engineering trade-offs</h2>
  <p>The blueprint favours clarity and repeatability over full production operational complexity; it is a reference starting point rather than a one-click platform install.</p>

  <p><a href="https://github.com/Lawrencechew/secure-aks-service-blueprint">View Source →</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
